# arch/arm64/configs/greatlte_base.config -- greatlte base: the gki_defconfig features Exynos 8895 greatlte
# cannot use (FULL_IMAGE_PLAN.md 2.5, WP-T). gl-build merges it FIRST, right after gki_defconfig and before
# L0's greatlte.config and the layer fragments (plan 2.2 T15), so a layer fragment can still turn any of these
# back on. "gki:N" = line N of A:arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig; "IK:N" = line N of the factory IKCONFIG
# (rewrite/work/factory/boot/ikconfig, the stock Pie kernel). Sizes: FULL_IMAGE_PLAN.md Appendix Z 0.S2
# (text+rodata+data+eh_frame of the L0 build objects each item removes) and the commit message.
# No comment line in this file may begin with the Kconfig "not set" form: merge_config.sh and gl-verify V1
# read such a line as a setting (A:scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh:119-120, A:scripts/kconfig/confdata.c:415-428).

# ---- image-wide: no shadow call stack (plan 1.2 X-33; also L6B D-5 and L6T R-T7: the camera DDK blob and
# EL3 clobber x18). Also drops .eh_frame: UNWIND_PATCH_PAC_INTO_SCS "depends on SHADOW_CALL_STACK" and
# "select UNWIND_TABLES" (A:arch/arm64/Kconfig:2396-2402); .eh_frame is kept only #ifdef CONFIG_UNWIND_TABLES
# (A:arch/arm64/kernel/vmlinux.lds.S:151-157). Stock had no SCS (4.4). gki:106, gki:74.
# CONFIG_SHADOW_CALL_STACK is not set
# CONFIG_UNWIND_PATCH_PAC_INTO_SCS is not set

# ---- KVM STAYS ON (user request 2026-09-28: LineageOS 23.2 / Android 16 ships packages/modules/Virtualization,
# whose backends are kvm, gunyah and genie; Exynos falls in the kvm category). gki:102-103 keep
# CONFIG_VIRTUALIZATION=y and CONFIG_KVM=y; VSOCKETS (gki:311) and VHOST_VSOCK (gki:640) stay with it, because
# they are the host side of the AVF VM transport. On this phone every CPU enters at EL1 (L0 logs "CPU: All
# CPU(s) started at EL1"; Samsung's uH/RKP owns EL2, IK:425-426 CONFIG_RKP=y CONFIG_UH_RKP=y, IK:5088 stock
# had no VIRTUALIZATION), so kvm_arm_init() prints "HYP mode not available" and returns -ENODEV
# (A:arch/arm64/kvm/arm.c:3008-3011): /dev/kvm never appears and AVF reports VMs as unsupported. This is the
# L0 behaviour (images 0001-0008 ran with KVM=y). To trim it later (0.S2: 1,258,065 B), write the Kconfig
# "not set" lines for KVM, VSOCKETS and VHOST_VSOCK here; the GKI_HIDDEN block below is already what KVM=n
# needs to build (0.S3).
# Gunyah is Qualcomm's hypervisor (A:drivers/virt/gunyah/Kconfig:9-17, "imply GUNYAH_QCOM_PLATFORM if
# ARCH_QCOM"); nothing on Exynos talks to it. gki:633.
# CONFIG_GUNYAH is not set

# ---- GKI-only hidden selects: GKI_HACKS_TO_FIX exists to pre-select helpers for modules built out of tree
# against a different config (A:init/Kconfig.gki:325-366, help "Unless you are building a GKI kernel to be used
# with modules built from a different config, say N here"). This image is monolithic (plan 2.5, no module on
# any partition): every in-tree driver selects what it uses. The GKI_HIDDEN_* options have prompts, so
# olddefconfig keeps them y once GKI_HACKS_TO_FIX is gone unless each one is unset (0.S3; the 28 entries of
# A:init/Kconfig.gki:1-296). WIRELESS_EXT (GKI_LEGACY_WEXT_ALLCONFIG, :174-181) matches L6D 6.1 (WEXT off).
# gki:126.
# CONFIG_GKI_HACKS_TO_FIX is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_DRM_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_MCP251XFD_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_REGMAP_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_CRYPTO_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_SND_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_SND_SOC_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_UFS_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_MMC_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_GPIO_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_X86_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_QCOM_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_MTK_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_MEDIA_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_VIRTUAL_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_LEGACY_WEXT_ALLCONFIG is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_USB_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_SOC_BUS_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_RPMSG_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_GPU_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_IRQ_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_HYPERVISOR_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_NET_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_PHY_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_MM_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_ETHERNET_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_IOMMU_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_DMA_CONFIGS is not set
# CONFIG_GKI_HIDDEN_XFRM_OFFLOAD_CONFIGS is not set

# ---- sanitizers: KASAN in gki is the hardware-tag mode (gki:817-818), which needs MTE (ARMv8.5,
# A:lib/Kconfig.kasan:123-131); both clusters are ARMv8.0 (A53 MIDR 0x410fd034, M2 MIDR 0x534f0010, L0 logs),
# so it only costs code. UBSAN (gki:808-809) instruments every object. Stock: IK:5144 no KASAN.
# CONFIG_KASAN is not set
# CONFIG_UBSAN is not set
# Data symbols in kallsyms: backtraces need text symbols only. tooling.config (merged last) turns it back on
# for every bring-up image (%ps in heartbeat lines, T 6.1). gki:54.
# CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL is not set

# ---- other SoC families and their blocks (gki:57-59, 333-336, 610-613, 489, 451, 437-447, 621-622,
# 99-100, 344-345, 506, 605-606, 528). The 8895 blocks are Exynos UART (samsung_tty), UFS (ufs-exynos),
# DW MMC, ACPM (not SCMI/SCPI) and the S2MPS17 PMIC's RTC (rtc-s5m, L7 5.10); plan 2.5.
